=== PARITY (vs web ClimateHistoryWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (ClimateHistorySource ->
    ClimateHistoryModel): useClimateHistory, useVehicles, useUnits, useDateFormat,
    useTranslation. Production wires the source over the KMP VehicleSystemsStore
    (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<[ClimateState]>>) + the settings UnitStore; the view performs
    NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection -> ClimateHistoryProjectionBuilder.build is a faithful port of web `buildChartData`:
    keep rows with a time (`created_at || timestamp`), convert insideTemp/outsideTemp (SI Celsius ->
    display via convertTempFromSI), sort ascending by time. Latest-value scan per series (newest-first,
    skip nils = web `latestInside`/`latestOutside`). y-axis envelope derived. Verified by EXECUTED
    XCTest (12 adapter + 2 format).
  Composition -> WidgetShell-equivalent chrome (ThermometerSun icon + "Climate History" title +
    freshness chip + refresh + optional Open) · stat row (Cabin/Outside latest + unit) · the chart.
    Recharts AreaChart -> Swift Charts: two AreaMarks (gradient 0.3->0 fill, unstacked so Cabin and
    Outside overlap rather than sum) + 2-pt LineMark strokes, monotone interpolation, gaps bridged
    (web `connectNulls`). Compact (cols<=1) renders the stat row only; wide (cols>=3) adds denser
    ticks + the unit title — matching the web `isCompact`/`isWide` branches.
  Shared components -> reuses the REAL apps/apple library compiled in GATE [1]/[2]: Color.TS, Font.TS,
    TSSpacing, TSRadius (tokens), chart-series color tokens, TSSkeleton (loading), ContentUnavailableView
    (empty). Recharts->Swift Charts; Leaflet->none. Color tokens map the web hex: Cabin #f97316 (orange)
    -> chartSeriesEnergy (the amber energy token, nearest hue in the palette); Outside #3b82f6 ->
    chartSeriesSpeed (an EXACT-hex match). The warm/cool contrast of the web source is preserved.
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton stat row + chart block) · empty ("No climate history" +
    ThermometerSun + hint) · error (retry) · stale (chip + banner, cached chart stays) · offline (chip +
    banner, cached chart) · content. Model phase resolution keeps cached values visible behind
    refresh/errors, matching the web shell (which never hides the chart on background error).
  i18n -> all 4 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.climateHistory.title, .cabin, .outside, .noData -> ALL PRESENT in ClimateHistoryWidget.strings
    (+ registry widget.climateHistory/.description + native chrome + a11y). No English literals in native
    code (temperature unit symbol °C/°F comes from the ClimateTemperatureUnit enum rawValue).
  a11y -> the chart is one element with a localized label + a state-summary value
    (ClimateHistoryAccessibility.summary: latest Cabin/Outside + unit); every button (refresh / retry /
    open) and stat column has an accessibilityLabel; Dynamic Type via tokens; TSSkeleton shimmer honors
    Reduce Motion.
  Telemetry -> ClimateHistoryModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"ClimateHistoryWidget") -> bridges
    shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (EXECUTED).
  Registry -> ClimateHistoryWidget.registration: id "climate-history", category "climate", default 2x4,
    min 2x4, max 4x40 (+ clamp()), matching registry/climate.ts. Asserted (EXECUTED).

  PARITY NOTE (y-axis floor — documented, Honesty rule 9): unlike the sibling pressure-history widget,
    temperature legitimately goes sub-zero (°C below freezing, and °F), so the projection's y-domain is
    NOT floored at 0 — it pads symmetrically around the real data min/max. A regression test
